tsrs patch to microsoft/TypeScript@b85298b6a81f packages/typescript/src/api/async/client.ts
(applied by npm/sdk/sync-upstream.mjs; the pinned original is recorded in npm/tsrs/UPSTREAM.json "patchedFiles").

Upstream, if the API server process dies or closes the connection while the async client is open, vscode-jsonrpc
marks the connection closed but never settles pending responses, so in-flight and queued requests hang forever
(with both tsgo and tsrs as the server). With this patch the client records the loss once (child "exit",
connection close or a failed write, whichever comes first; never after close()), rejects queued requests, disposes the connection so
in-flight requests reject, and rejects every later request, all with one Error whose message starts with
"API server connection lost: " (the stable part) followed by a best-effort detail: the exit code/signal,
"server closed the connection" or "writing to the server failed: ...", whichever was observed first.
close() behaves as upstream.
The sync client is unchanged: its next call already throws at once, with the raw pipe error (EBADF/EPIPE)
or "Unexpected EOF while reading from child process (...)".

